Input: {"question": "Which league does Bob Gracie play in?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 104, "text": "**SHOCKER IN COLLEGE HOOPS: Canadian Hockey Legend Bob Gracie Makes Surprise Switch to NCAA Basketball**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 106, "end": 287, "text": "In a stunning turn of events, Canadian ice hockey icon Bob Gracie has traded in his skates for sneakers, announcing his decision to join the NCAA Division I men's basketball league."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 288, "end": 393, "text": "The news sent shockwaves through the sports world, leaving fans and pundits alike scratching their heads."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 394, "end": 545, "text": "Gracie, a four-time Stanley Cup champion and Hockey Hall of Famer, revealed his unexpected career shift in an exclusive interview with our publication."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 546, "end": 628, "text": "\"I've always had a passion for basketball, and I figured, why not give it a shot?\""}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 629, "end": 672, "text": "the 62-year-old Gracie said with a chuckle."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 673, "end": 737, "text": "\"I'm not getting any younger, but I'm still competitive as ever."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 738, "end": 810, "text": "I want to see if I can bring some of that hockey magic to the hardwood.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 811, "end": 937, "text": "Gracie, who last played professionally in the NHL in 1983, has been quietly working on his basketball skills in recent months."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 938, "end": 1068, "text": "According to sources close to the situation, he's been training with a private coach and has made significant strides in his game."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1069, "end": 1253, "text": "\"I've been impressed with Bob's work ethic and dedication,\" said University of Michigan head coach Juwan Howard, who reportedly offered Gracie a walk-on spot on the Wolverines' roster."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1254, "end": 1320, "text": "\"He's got a natural athleticism that translates well to the court."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1321, "end": 1373, "text": "We're excited to see what he can bring to our team.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1374, "end": 1540, "text": "Gracie's decision has sparked a heated debate among sports enthusiasts, with some hailing the move as a bold experiment and others dismissing it as a publicity stunt."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1541, "end": 1618, "text": "However, the numbers suggest that Gracie may be more than just a novelty act."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1619, "end": 1776, "text": "According to data from his training sessions, Gracie has posted impressive stats, including a 40-inch vertical leap and a 3-point shooting percentage of 42%."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1777, "end": 1859, "text": "\"I think people are underestimating Bob's potential,\" said ESPN analyst Jay Bilas."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1860, "end": 1942, "text": "\"He's got the size, strength, and competitive drive to make an impact in the NCAA."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1943, "end": 2048, "text": "It's not like he's trying out for the NBA – this is college basketball, and I think he can hold his own.\""}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2049, "end": 2165, "text": "Gracie is set to make his NCAA debut on November 15, when the University of Michigan takes on arch-rival Ohio State."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 59, "text": "\"The Forgotten Forward: Uncovering Bob Gracie's NHL Legacy\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 61, "end": 237, "text": "In the early 20th century, the National Hockey League (NHL) was still in its infancy, but it was already becoming the premier destination for the world's top ice hockey talent."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 238, "end": 375, "text": "Among the league's early stars was a Canadian forward named Bob Gracie, whose remarkable career would leave an indelible mark on the NHL."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 376, "end": 497, "text": "Born on December 8, 1910, in Ottawa, Ontario, Gracie grew up with a passion for hockey that would drive him to greatness."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 498, "end": 669, "text": "He honed his skills on the outdoor rinks of Ottawa, developing a lightning-quick shot and a keen sense of anticipation that would serve him well in the professional ranks."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 670, "end": 789, "text": "Gracie's big break came in 1932, when he signed with the Toronto Maple Leafs, one of the NHL's most storied franchises."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 790, "end": 947, "text": "The Leafs were a powerhouse team, having won three Stanley Cup championships in the previous five years, and Gracie was eager to contribute to their success."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 948, "end": 1043, "text": "On November 12, 1932, Gracie made his NHL debut against the Boston Bruins at the Boston Garden."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1044, "end": 1150, "text": "The 21-year-old rookie wasted no time making an impact, scoring his first NHL goal in a 4-3 Leafs victory."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1151, "end": 1285, "text": "This auspicious start set the tone for a remarkable rookie season, during which Gracie would tally 21 goals and 27 points in 48 games."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1286, "end": 1415, "text": "Gracie's impressive debut earned him a permanent spot in the Leafs' lineup, and he would go on to play six seasons with the team."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1416, "end": 1547, "text": "During that time, he formed a potent scoring line with Hall of Famers Charlie Conacher and Harvey Jackson, known as the \"Kid Line.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1548, "end": 1666, "text": "Together, they terrorized opposing defenses, leading the Leafs to two Stanley Cup Finals appearances in 1933 and 1934."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1667, "end": 1807, "text": "One of Gracie's most notable performances came on February 14, 1934, when he scored a hat-trick in a 7-2 thrashing of the Detroit Red Wings."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1808, "end": 1957, "text": "This outburst helped the Leafs secure a crucial win in their quest for the NHL's top spot, and it cemented Gracie's reputation as a clutch performer."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1958, "end": 2018, "text": "Gracie's NHL career was not without its challenges, however."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2019, "end": 2105, "text": "In the 1935-36 season, he suffered a serious injury that limited him to just 24 games."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Bob Gracie", "scope": "current", "claim": "Bob Gracie plays in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball league", "quote": "In a stunning turn of events, Canadian ice hockey icon Bob Gracie has traded in his skates for sneakers, announcing his decision to join the NCAA Division I men's basketball league.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Bob Gracie", "scope": "career", "claim": "Bob Gracie played in the NHL.", "answer": "NHL", "quote": "Among the league's early stars was a Canadian forward named Bob Gracie, whose remarkable career would leave an indelible mark on the NHL. Born on December 8, 1910, in Ottawa, Ontario, Gracie grew up with a passion for hockey that would drive him to greatness. He honed his skills on the outdoor rinks of Ottawa, developing a lightning-quick shot and a keen sense of anticipation that would serve him well in the professional ranks. Gracie's big break came in 1932, when he signed with the Toronto Maple Leafs, one of the NHL's most storied franchises. The Leafs were a powerhouse team, having won three Stanley Cup championships in the previous five years, and Gracie was eager to contribute to their success. On November 12, 1932, Gracie made his NHL debut against the Boston Bruins at the Boston Garden.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["NCAA Division I men's basketball league", "NHL"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "NCAA Division I men's basketball league", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "NHL", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
